module

-- The root of the `@MINI@` library: the same calculus as `@CALCULUS@`, reduced
-- to a handful of rules.
--
-- Its whole purpose is build time. The full package takes minutes to elaborate
-- and its proofs take hours; this one takes seconds, so a proof about the
-- checker itself -- an invariant, a preservation lemma, the soundness argument
-- -- can be developed against it and moved over once it holds.
--
-- It is compiled from the same signature by
-- `install/install-@CALCLOWER@.sh --mini`, with `--rules` naming the subset and
-- no parser. So it is not a different calculus: it is the same one with fewer
-- rules, which is what makes a proof developed here worth moving.
--
-- Logos does exactly this with `CpcMini`, and reports the payoff bluntly: its
-- `Proofs/Checker.lean` is byte-identical to `Cpc`'s, and the two packages
-- differ in rule set, signature *and* required invariants. A proof that holds
-- for both is one that did not quietly depend on the calculus.
--
-- No executable and no parser: nothing here reads a proof file.
public import @MINI@.@CHECKER@
import all @MINI@.@CHECKER@
public import @MINI@.SmtEval
import all @MINI@.SmtEval
public import @MINI@.SmtModel
import all @MINI@.SmtModel
public import @MINI@.Spec
import all @MINI@.Spec

-- The proofs under `@MINI@/Proofs/` are deliberately not imported here: build
-- them directly, which is the point of having this package at all.

public section
